course: dictionary
lesson: 93
title: Adaptation: built for home
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An adaptation is a feature that helps a living thing survive in its habitat. The feature can be a body part, like a camel's hump, or a behaviour, like the way an animal acts. A habitat is the place where a living thing lives.
explain: Look for the clues. «Ducks have webbed feet» tells you the feet are useful, and webbed means the toes are joined by skin, which helps a duck push through water. Ask yourself: does this feature help the living thing survive where it lives? If it does, it is an adaptation.
explain: Adaptations do not happen in one animal's life. «Adaptations develop over many generations, not in one animal's life.» A generation is one set of parents, then their young, then their young's young. Changes build up slowly over many of these.
explain: Adaptation has other meanings too. A film made from a book is an adaptation of that book, and a process of changing to fit a new situation is also called adaptation. Use the words around it, such as habitat, generations or film, to decide which meaning fits.
fact: An adaptation is a feature of a living thing that helps it survive in its habitat.
fact: Cacti store water in deserts, so they can survive where it is very dry.
fact: Owls have big eyes for seeing at night.
fact: Arctic foxes turn white in winter, which helps them hide in the snow.
fact: Adaptations develop over many generations, and this slow change is called evolution.
exercise: Which of these is an adaptation that helps a duck survive? | A pond with weeds in it | *Webbed feet for swimming | The sound of rain | A duck's name
exercise: «Many films are adaptations of books, comics or games.» What does adaptation mean here? | A feature that helps an animal hide | A slow change over many lives | A kind of desert plant | *A changed version of something, like a film made from a book
exercise: «Adaptations develop over many generations, not in one animal's life.» Which statement is true? | Adaptations happen in a single day | Only plants can have adaptations | One animal can fully adapt in its own lifetime | *Adaptations build up over many generations
test: Arctic foxes turn white in winter. Why is this an adaptation? | It makes them warmer in summer | *It helps them hide in the snow | It shows that they are old | It is a film about foxes
test: Adaptation can mean a process of changing to fit a new situation. Which sentence uses this meaning? | The film was an adaptation of the novel | *Over time, the fish adapted to the dirty water | The camel has a hump | The owl has big eyes
exam: Owls have big eyes for seeing at night. What does this show? | An owl that is very old | *An adaptation that helps them survive in the dark | A film adaptation of an owl story | A habitat that is wet
